WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.860
Hey, welcome back to 40 Days of Holiness. This is day 31.

2
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.240
We're talking about holiness as beholding glory.

3
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.020
God's glory is like a mega theme of scripture.

4
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.800
God is passionately committed to his own glorious,

5
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.860
brilliant awesomeness, his unique glory to be shining

6
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.720
out and seen and rejoiced in. And this glory is beautifully, intimately

7
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.340
connected in scripture to holiness.

8
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.200
In fact, glory and holiness are used parallel a lot of times in scripture.

9
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.400
God's glory is holy, and his holiness is glorious.

10
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.949
So in 2 Corinthians 3, Paul is writing about the

11
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.870
glory of God's holiness and how that glory and

12
00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:50.660
holiness is produced in us. And he makes this comparison that's

13
00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:54.600
really interesting between the law of the old covenant of the law and the

14
00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.780
new covenant of grace. So let's look at it in 2 Corinthians

15
00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.720
3:7. "Now if the ministry that brought death, which

16
00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:06.440
was engraved in letters on stone, came with glory

17
00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.840
so that the Israelites could not look steadily at the face of Moses

18
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:11.890
because of its glory,

19
00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.650
transitory though it was." So here's the idea.

20
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.950
Moses was in the presence of God, the glorious, holy,

21
00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:23.720
face-to-face presence of God. And like a fire

22
00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.520
poker that you plunge into the glory of the fire, and you leave it there for a

23
00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.420
long time, you take it out, and the glory and power and light of the fire

24
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.020
has gotten into the poker, and it's glowing like the fire.

25
00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.140
In the same way, Moses has been plunged into the glorious

26
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.040
face-to-face presence of face of God, and he comes down from the mountain, and his

27
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.890
face is glowing. But I want you to notice that Paul says that

28
00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.200
this was the ministry that brought death.

29
00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:53.280
In other words, the law of God, because of the sinfulness

30
00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.350
of our character, even though the law was good and holy,

31
00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:58.620
there was glory in it.

32
00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:03.080
Still, the law brought spiritual death to us

33
00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.500
because we didn't have the ability to make ourselves holy

34
00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.820
by our own efforts.

35
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.880
So the law could command holiness, but it did not have the

36
00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:18.880
power of Christ's blood to produce holiness in

37
00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.930
us. So it could reveal and command holiness, but

38
00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.560
it could not empower and produce it.

39
00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.260
Verse number eight,

40
00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:29.930
"Will not the ministry of the Spirit be even more glorious?

41
00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:33.640
If the ministry that brought condemnation was glorious,

42
00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.460
how much more glorious is the ministry that brings

43
00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:38.280
righteousness?"

44
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.080
So he says here that another way of God dealing with his people,

45
00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.800
a new covenant, has come along, has been revealed,

46
00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.040
and we expect it to have glory as well because it came from a glorious

47
00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:55.020
God. And he says we should expect even more of God's

48
00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:58.660
holy glory in this new covenant because it has the power to

49
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.820
produce righteousness instead of death.

50
00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.960
Verse 10, "For what was glorious now has no glory in

51
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.200
comparison with the surpassing glory.

52
00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.460
And if what was transitory came with glory, how much greater is the

53
00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.220
glory of that which is lasting? Therefore, since we have such a

54
00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.240
hope, we are very bold. We are not like Moses, who would put

55
00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.020
a veil over his face to prevent the Israelites from seeing the

56
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.600
end, the result of what was passing away."

57
00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.580
Moses veiled his face because the Israelites couldn't stand the brilliance of

58
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.060
the glory of God on his face. They were not saved, and they were fearful.

59
00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:39.540
They were scared. Moses had to veil his face to keep them from freaking

60
00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.290
out. Verse 14, "But their minds were made dull,

61
00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.220
for to this day, the same veil remains when the old

62
00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:51.060
covenant is read. It has not been removed because only

63
00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:55.120
in Christ is it taken away. Even to this day when Moses is

64
00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:59.080
read, a veil covers their hearts. But whenever anyone turns

65
00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.920
to the Lord, the veil is taken away.

66
00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.769
Now the Lord is the Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is freedom."

67
00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:10.360
Now, he's going to talk about how the Spirit produces this holiness in

68
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.040
us. Look at verse 18. All right, you ready?

69
00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:15.980
"And we all who with unveiled faces

70
00:04:16.399 --> 00:04:20.380
contemplate the Lord's glory are being transformed into

71
00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:24.370
his image with ever-increasing glory." What is

72
00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.850
the image of God? Jesus? What is it? It's holiness.

73
00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.880
And when we look and contemplate, the word here in Greek is

74
00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:33.820
steadfastly look into a mirror.

75
00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.150
We are changed. So the old covenant had the law, the new has

76
00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:41.960
grace. The old had our efforts, the new has faith.

77
00:04:42.469 --> 00:04:45.400
The old had death, but this one has righteousness.

78
00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:49.000
The old one had bondage, and this one has

79
00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:52.940
freedom. The old one was hiding. This new one

80
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.920
is beholding. The old one was despair.

81
00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.260
This new one is transformation. And the old

82
00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.080
one was fading. This one's on its way down.

83
00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.260
This one is on its way up.

84
00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.880
This one is going away. This one's coming on strong.

85
00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:14.020
This one hasn't the power to do anything but reveal and command

86
00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:17.820
holiness. This one can empower and actually

87
00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.880
produce holiness in our lives. So

88
00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:24.220
I want to take a second here and just say, remember,

89
00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:30.110
some people look at this covenant, and

90
00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.380
they act like, and they talk like we're still living

91
00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:37.320
here, like we have to try harder and all that sort of thing.

92
00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:41.230
And other people, they say, "Well, we don't have to try hard anymore," but they

93
00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.900
forget that there's a new covenant that doesn't just

94
00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.100
reveal and command holiness and then leave us stuck and

95
00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.870
powerless. It actually empowers and produces

96
00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.700
that holiness, literally produces that holiness in our life.

97
00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.520
We are being transformed into the same image, and it

98
00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.420
is increasing in glory.

99
00:06:02.368 --> 00:06:05.368
So you and I, if you want to increase in holiness,

100
00:06:06.368 --> 00:06:10.178
you need to look up to Christ, look up to Jesus, and

101
00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:12.948
consider his holiness, and think of him.

102
00:06:12.988 --> 00:06:16.888
This is why the writer to the Hebrews says that we ought to look unto

103
00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:19.508
Jesus, the author and the finisher of our faith,

104
00:06:20.428 --> 00:06:23.848
and we ought to look to him even when we're in hard times.

105
00:06:24.048 --> 00:06:27.858
Looking to Jesus and beholding and meditating on him, thinking on him,

106
00:06:28.508 --> 00:06:31.048
produces his image in us.

107
00:06:31.948 --> 00:06:35.368
We are transformed into his image.

108
00:06:35.408 --> 00:06:39.018
Whereas Moses' glory was always fading, ours is always

109
00:06:39.048 --> 00:06:42.918
increasing. Whereas Moses' glory from being in the presence of God

110
00:06:43.328 --> 00:06:46.418
was always growing less because it was fading away,

111
00:06:47.308 --> 00:06:51.068
ours is always getting greater. Whereas they had to be afraid to look

112
00:06:51.168 --> 00:06:55.108
steadfastly at Christ, we do not have to be afraid because

113
00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:58.848
Christ doesn't just command and reveal holiness, he empowers and

114
00:06:58.888 --> 00:07:02.428
produces it when we look and behold and keep our

115
00:07:02.508 --> 00:07:05.488
eyes fixed on Jesus and his rulership.

116
00:07:06.207 --> 00:07:10.008
So the temptation sometimes is to produce holiness by saying,

117
00:07:10.428 --> 00:07:12.028
"I'm going to look to my efforts."

118
00:07:13.288 --> 00:07:15.008
Right? "I'm going to look to my intellect.

119
00:07:15.648 --> 00:07:17.468
I'm going to look to my trying harder.

120
00:07:17.908 --> 00:07:19.788
I'm going to look to my self-discipline.

121
00:07:19.808 --> 00:07:21.618
I'm going to look to my willpower."

122
00:07:22.488 --> 00:07:24.488
But I would tell you that

123
00:07:24.608 --> 00:07:28.268
self-noticing does not particularly produce holiness.

124
00:07:29.008 --> 00:07:32.948
You do have to consider yourself for a little while sometimes, but the deepest part

125
00:07:32.988 --> 00:07:36.308
of holiness and the transformation that happens is when we are considering

126
00:07:36.708 --> 00:07:40.688
Christ. It is not in moments of self-remembrance that we grow.

127
00:07:41.148 --> 00:07:45.038
It is in moments of self-forgetfulness, when we see Christ and

128
00:07:45.068 --> 00:07:45.808
we say, "Oh,

129
00:07:46.968 --> 00:07:47.888
look at who he is,"

130
00:07:48.728 --> 00:07:52.368
and we take on the glow. We plunged into the

131
00:07:52.408 --> 00:07:55.718
glorious presence and holiness of God, come out glowing,

132
00:07:56.388 --> 00:07:59.148
and that's an increasing glory that's producing more and more

133
00:07:59.168 --> 00:08:01.068
holiness. I'll see you tomorrow.
